{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨4,1,4⟩$ and $q=⟨2,3,3⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{22}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1eba6a576eabee5331237f47195bdc5c2e609298fe273718e1b4dc2d39aa3541"} {"question" "q-19142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{22}{\\sqrt{23}}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{2\\sqrt{11}}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{3\\sqrt{11}}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{22}}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{33}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{22}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-1,2,\\sqrt{11}⟩$ and $b=⟨4,3,\\sqrt{11}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3+\\sqrt{11}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{11})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(\\sqrt{11})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{13}{6}-\\frac{13}{4} \\\\  & =13(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =13(\\frac{2}{12}-\\frac{3}{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1eba6a576eabee5331237f47195bdc5c2e609298fe273718e1b4dc2d39aa3541"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{12}{13}"] ["math" "-\\frac{13}{12}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{12}{13}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-19146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{13}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 15+0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+5\\cdot x \\\\  & =5x-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 5x-30 & =0 \\\\ 5x & =30 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1eba6a576eabee5331237f47195bdc5c2e609298fe273718e1b4dc2d39aa3541"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4+x\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =14-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 14-2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =14 \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1eba6a576eabee5331237f47195bdc5c2e609298fe273718e1b4dc2d39aa3541"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-237015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-318987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $m=⟨6,8,0⟩$ and $n=⟨0,5,12⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-318987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{n}_{x}^{2}+{n}_{y}^{2}+{n}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6)(0)+(8)(5)+(0)(12)}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{169}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,m\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{m}_{x}^{2}+{m}_{y}^{2}+{m}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{100}} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n & =\\frac{40}{13}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{40-52}{13} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-318987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1eba6a576eabee5331237f47195bdc5c2e609298fe273718e1b4dc2d39aa3541"} {"question" "q-318987" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"} {"question" "q-318987" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{12}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073634/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f54267c12b6aa5cd371f379a8c4ca9cfd7f1e2213f758854e4fb78b804f40d3"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2706 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
